# Luminary marker — fix harness tests broken by cli#245 file-fallback

- date: 2026-09-26
- branch: fix/harness-file-fallback-test-isolation
- lead: michael-feathers
- supporting: [kent-beck]
- primary_lens: michael-feathers
- compatibility_anchor: linus-torvalds
- reason: test-side characterization needs to survive real runner state (file-fallback creates env drift the tests must isolate from)

## Why these lenses

**Lead — @luminary michael-feathers.** Characterization tests pin behavior. When a new code path (file-fallback) changes the env the existing tests read, the tests need to isolate their env explicitly. Set `CLAUDE_OAUTH_TOKEN_FILE=/dev/null` so the test controls the input rather than inheriting the runner's HOME state.

**Supporting — @luminary kent-beck.** Tier 0 tests should be hermetic. The fix restores the hermetic property by overriding the fallback path.

**Compatibility anchor — @luminary linus-torvalds.** Adopter contract stays intact — no runtime behavior changes, only tests get more isolated.
